[step] These are the two 0.3 mm deep outboard station-reference grooves in the rear face of the donor block. Each is 0.8 mm wide and 6 mm high, centred at tube height. They sit outside the complete Ø30 fixed-pad bearing disks; the uncut contact planes stay at X−26. The groove floor has 25.7 mm of axial stock behind it.
alternatives: An entirely flush face with ink-only marks removes the grooves but loses the permanent outboard reference after cleaning the ink away. A wider or deeper groove makes the reference larger while removing more stock beside the outboard edge, without enlarging the backed bearing disks.
file: hardware/printed-parts/fixtures/tube-insertion/tube-insertion-base.step
click: x=-25.700 y=57.250 z=30.000
click: x=-25.700 y=-39.750 z=30.000

[sliver] These six narrow faces are the floors and side walls of the two shallow station-reference grooves. A 0.3 mm groove side face or 0.8 mm floor is a recess surface, not a freestanding strip of that thickness. Each floor retains 25.7 mm axial backing in the 26 mm block. The grooves lie outside the Ø30 factory-pad contact areas.
alternatives: Omitting the grooves gives a flush face but removes its permanent reference. Increasing their width or depth enlarges the recess rather than thickening a load member; the primary bearing planes and full pad backing are already continuous.
file: hardware/printed-parts/fixtures/tube-insertion/tube-insertion-base.step
