[ledge] These 0.24 mm² downward faces close the tops of the two shallow reference grooves at Z33. Their unsupported axial reach is only the 0.3 mm groove depth, backed by the donor block; they are not projecting bearing lips. The native base slice emits no support for these local recess ends.
alternatives: Extending each groove to the top edge removes its closing face but adds a much longer recess without helping pad alignment. A flush face removes the permanent references. Enlarging the ledge means deepening the recess and removing additional block stock.
file: hardware/printed-parts/fixtures/tube-insertion/tube-insertion-base.step
